Approved: revision 17, 2026-08-03, at 9bc2c1964 (27 FRs / 10 NFRs / 50 ACs / 122 normative bullets).

Revisions 16 and 17 were made during the design phase, in response to round 2 of the design review.
Revision 16 carried design decision 2 (the AddBrighterAspNetCoreScopes -> AddBrighterRequestScope
rename, alignment) and design decision 4 (FR-22.4, an Error for an opt-in defeated by an
application's own IBrighterOptions registration — new scope, and therefore a new AC, AC-50).

Because revision 16 was more than alignment, it had its own review round, per the requirement
owner's standing rule. That round returned 11 findings, 9 at or above threshold 60, none Critical
(review-requirements.md). It confirmed that every codebase claim in the new material holds against
source, and that the rename was complete and correct. Revision 17 closes all nine, plus two
below-threshold items rule 4 itself caused.

One owner decision was taken in that round: FR-22.4 covers BOTH registration orderings. An
application IBrighterOptions registered before Brighter wins the TryAddSingleton; one registered
after wins resolution as the last descriptor. Either way the object the factories read is not
Brighter's and the affinity override is never applied. Consequence, carried into FR-22.4: detecting
the defeat at the point Brighter's own TryAddSingleton finds the service already present sees only
the before ordering and is not on its own sufficient — this widens what the design's sixth
scope-configuration rule must evaluate.

Approved without a further review round: the nine findings closed cleanly, none was Critical, and
the substantive rewrites (AC-50, FR-22.4) were verified against source and against the document's
own conventions for error-rule Acceptance Criteria.

This supersedes the revision-15 approval, which this file recorded.
